  "prose": [
    {
      "section": null,
      "line": 39,
      "afterExample": null,
      "text": "### Structure\n\nDrawer is a grid layout that can show/hide a sidebar on the left or right side of the page, based on the screen size or based on the value of a `drawer-toggle` checkbox.  \nDrawer must be the parent element of the content and sidebar."
    },
    {
      "section": null,
      "line": 55,
      "afterExample": null,
      "text": "### Functionality\n\nDrawer sidebar is hidden by default.\nYou can make it visible on larger screens using `lg:drawer-open` class (or using other responsive prefixes: sm, md, lg, xl)\n\nYou can check/uncheck the checkbox using JavaScript or by clicking the `label` tag which is assigned to the hidden checkbox\n\n> :INFO:\n>\n> Opening a drawer adds a [scrollbar-gutter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/scrollbar-gutter) to the page to avoid layout shift on operating systems that have a fixed scrollbar.\n> On recent Chromium based browsers vertical scrollbar presence is detected automatically. On Safari and on mobile devices the scrollbar is displayed as overlay so there will not be gutter. On Firefox you need to detect the presence of vertical scrollbar and set the `scrollbar-gutter: stable` or `scrollbar-gutter: unset` on `:root` element yourself.\n> If you don't want to use this feature, [you can exclude `rootscrollgutter`](/docs/config/#exclude)."
    }
  ],
